From 307134c67e10474daa5696664a6a01c2bab5f7d0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c1t1zen1 <kmkennedy@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 17:24:56 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] Roof Road: keep the stage-2 route on its legs and finishable

The 13-mouth extension (17c9cae) left pieces running across the new
corners and an autopilot stall at s=1232. Numbers in level.js, plus a
corner deck at each new corner:

- Leg 13's temple wall, street props and porches ended at rail.length,
  which now means the end of leg 21: one 665 m straight wall and props
  across corners 13-20. They end at the end of leg 13 again.
- Straight transition balconies (and the castle keep) sat across the
  fillets of corners 13-20. A corner deck is the one piece that follows
  a turn, as at corners 1-12: K13 (already built), new decks at 14 and
  15 at the balconies' 4.5 m, and at 16-20 level with their balconies.
  The balconies stay, each on its own leg.
- 'theater 2' ran to the end of leg 15 under six newer houses; its
  4.5 m ridge tied with theirs, so the runner never stood on them (the
  stall). It ends before 'drama school' now.
- The leg 16-20 balconies sat at the 4.5 m of the long houses' ridges
  they overlap: the same tie. At 4.1 m they are a drop below the ridge.
- fPerch was routed twice, leaving a hole in the route numbers; the
  autopilot then stopped on the stage ridge, one short of the perch.
- Street props every 5.5 m on legs 17, 18, 19, 21 keep a climb-back
  within 12 m now the leg-13 props no longer run there.

rooftop_test 40/40; alley test passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
